<Project>

  <!--
    Override the NuGet-resolved Parquet.Net assembly (Parquet.dll) with the patched
    build that lives next to this file, also as Parquet.dll.

    SOURCE OF TRUTH for this binary: the `maccoss-developers` repo, path
    skylinedev/Parquet.Net6 - a SIBLING checkout under the same project root as pwiz,
    not a folder inside this repo. BUILD.md there says how it is built and
    PATCH-NOTES.md what it changes: upstream 6.1.0 plus the ThriftCompactProtocolReader
    struct-skip fix (a defensive read fix), a split of writing a column into preparing
    it in memory and appending it to the file (added public API; written bytes unchanged),
    and a fix to the narrow integer encoders, which were not safe to run concurrently.

    Every consumer references the NuGet package for its dependencies (ExcludeAssets="compile"),
    and compiles against and deploys the patched Parquet.dll here. The target below drops
    the package's own Parquet.dll from the copy-local items, which feed the build output,
    the publish folder and deps.json. Copying the patched dll over it after the build is
    not enough, because publishing copies the package's dll straight from the NuGet cache.
    Excluding the package's runtime assets is not an option either: NuGet applies that to
    its dependencies too. The patched dll has the same AssemblyVersion=6.0.0 as the stock
    6.1.0 NuGet release, so nothing warns until a call to the patched API fails.
    (It was checked in as ParquetNet.dll while a native parquet.dll, used by BiblioSpec,
    owned the plain name in Skyline's output folder. That native DLL is gone.)

    Imported by pwiz_tools/Directory.Build.targets and pwiz-sharp/Directory.Build.targets.

    A project that compiles against Parquet.Net sets ReferenceParquetNet=true and gets the
    pair below: the package for its dependency graph, and the patched build to compile
    against and deploy. The compile assets do not flow to a referencing project, so every
    project with Parquet code in it opts in for itself.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(ReferenceParquetNet)' == 'true'">
    <PackageReference Include="Parquet.Net" Version="6.1.0" ExcludeAssets="compile" />
    <!-- A full path, not "Parquet" with a HintPath: a simple name lets ResolveAssemblyReference
         bind to any Parquet.dll among a project's Content items first, and Skyline deploys
         BlibBuild's output folder as Content. -->
    <Reference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Parquet.dll">
      <Private>true</Private>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Unconditional, because a project that only references a ReferenceParquetNet project
       still gets the package's Parquet.dll transitively. -->
  <Target Name="RemoveNuGetParquetNet" AfterTargets="ResolvePackageAssets">
    <ItemGroup>
      <RuntimeCopyLocalItems Remove="@(RuntimeCopyLocalItems)"
                             Condition="'%(RuntimeCopyLocalItems.NuGetPackageId)' == 'Parquet.Net'" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
